{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":76434050,"ns":0,"title":"Dick Sandberg","revisions":[{"revid":1376175856,"parentid":1372595040,"minor":false,"timestamp":"2026-09-22T15:02:52Z","size":6025,"sha1":"16fa74805bbeb7266b5c672b7f75b245be9d351e","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Short description|Swedish professor and wood scientist (born 1967)}}\n{{Infobox scientist\n| name                  = Dick Sandberg\n| image                 = Dr. Dick Sandberg in Sopron in 2018.jpg\n| birth_date            = {{Birth date and age|1967|05|08}}\n| birth_place           = [[Söderhamn]]\n| awards         = Fellow of the [[International Academy of Wood Science|IAWS]] <small>(2021)</small><br />Editor of [[Wood Material Science and Engineering]] <small>(2012)</small>\n| education             = [[KTH Royal Institute of Technology]]\n| occupation            = {{Hlist|Researcher|educator|[[Wood science|wood scientist]]}}\n| years_active          = Since 1996\n}}\n'''Dick Sandberg''' ([[Söderhamn]], [[Sweden]], 8 May 1967)<ref>{{cite web |title= CV of Prof. Dr. Dick Sandberg - NTNU|url=https://backends.it.ntnu.no/user-profile-service/rest/files/0f3a10db-2bb3-30e5-bd43-bd5c24a56893 |access-date=6 Mar 2026}}</ref> is a Swedish mechanical engineer and [[Wood science|wood scientist]] at the Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU),<ref>https://www.ntnu.edu/employees/dick.sandberg Prof. Dick Sandberg, NTNU (Norway)</ref><ref>{{cite web | title=Sandberg, Dick (0000-0002-4526-9391) | website=Simple search| date=1 December 2023 | url=http://ltu.diva-portal.org/smash/person.jsf?pid=authority-person%3A39389&dswid=-6268 | ref={{sfnref | Simple search| 2023}} | access-date=24 March 2024}}</ref> who is an elected fellow (''FIAWS'') of the [[The International Academy of Wood Science|International Academy of Wood Science]].<ref>{{cite web | title=Fellows | website=The International Academy of Wood Science| date=14 November 2012 | url=https://www.iaws-web.org/fellows--dues/overview-of-fellows/ | ref={{sfnref | The International Academy of Wood Science| 2012}} | access-date=24 March 2024}}</ref>\n\nHe is currently the editor-in-chief at the journal [[Wood Material Science and Engineering]],<ref>https://www.tandfonline.com/action/journalInformation?show=editorialBoard&journalCode=swoo20 Editor: Prof. Dick Sandberg, journal \"Wood Material Science and Engineering\"</ref> and the period 2013–2024, he has served as a chair professor at the [[Luleå University of Technology]],<ref>{{cite web | title=Dick Sandberg | website=Luleå tekniska universitet | date=18 October 2023 | url=https://www.ltu.se/en/staff/d/dick-sandberg | access-date=24 March 2024}}</ref> Division of Wood Science and Engineering.\n\n== Career ==\nSandberg was born in [[Söderhamn]], Sweden. He obtained his PhD degree in mechanical engineering, with specialization in wood technology and processing from the [[KTH Royal Institute of Technology]] in Stockholm in 1998.\n\nAfterwards, he worked as a wood specialist and manager in several wood enterprises in Sweden, and later served as a professor in forest products at [[Linnaeus University]] in Växjö. In 2015, he was elected as a chaired professor at Wood Science and Engineering division of Luleå University of Technology, in [[Skellefteå]], where he worked until September 2024. \n\nHis main research interests include, among others, wood material properties, scanning technology and wood machining, as well as the production systems.<ref>{{cite web | title=EVA 4.0 | website=EVA 4.0 | url=https://eva.fld.czu.cz/en/r-13572-people/r-14414-sp-9-novel-wood-based-materials-related-to-gc-and-industry-4-0 | access-date=24 March 2024}}</ref> Until March 2024, he has published more than 300 research works in several international journals and conferences.\n[[File:Springer Handbook of Wood Science and Technology.jpg|120px|thumb|Springer Handbook of Wood Science and Technology]]\n\n== Recognition ==\nSince 2009, Sandberg has served as the editor-in-chief at the referred wood-related, scientific journal ''[[Wood Material Science and Engineering]]''<ref>https://www.tandfonline.com/action/journalInformation?show=editorialBoard&journalCode=swoo20 Editorial Board (Wood Material Science and Engineering</ref> of the [[Taylor & Francis]] Group. \n\nIn 2021, in recognition of his research work, he was elected as a ''[[fellow]]'' at [[the International Academy of Wood Science]]. In October 2023, a [[metascience|meta-research]] carried out by [[John Ioannidis]] et al. at [[Stanford University]] included Dick Sandberg in ''Elsevier Data 2022,'' where he was ranked in the top 2% of researchers of all time in wood science (''forestry – materials''), having a c-index of 2.9702.<ref>{{citation | last=Baas | first=Jeroen | title=October 2023 data-update for \"Updated science-wide author databases of standardized citation indicators\" | chapter=Bibliometrics |year=2023 | volume=6 | publisher=Elsevier Data Repository | doi=10.17632/BTCHXKTZYW.6 | url=https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/btchxktzyw/6 | access-date=2024-03-22}}</ref>\n\nIn 2023, along with wood scientists [[Alfred Teischinger]] and [[Peter Niemz]], he edited the referenced edition of [[Springer Science+Business Media|Springer]] ''Handbook of Wood Science and Technology''.<ref>{{cite book|title=Springer Handbooks|publisher=Springer International Publishing|isbn=978-3-030-81314-7|year=2023|chapter=Springer Handbook of Wood Science and Technology|publication-place=Cham|page=25-26|issn=2522-8692|doi=10.1007/978-3-030-81315-4|s2cid=257902863 }}</ref>\n\n== References ==\n{{reflist}}\n\n== External links ==\n* [http://www.innovawood.com/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=2G6BkDMEgh0%3D&tabid=494&mid=2325 LTU – Wood Science and Engineering]\n* [https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Dick-Sandberg ResearchGate]\n\n{{Authority control}}\n\n{{DEFAULTSORT:Sandberg, Dick}}\n[[Category:20th-century Swedish scientists]]\n[[Category:Fellows 